   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing as a lipopeptide with a depsipeptide ring. I assigned each stereocentre from its wedge or hash by working out CIP priorities.\n\n**Sequence, left to right:**\n- A 4-methylhexanoyl chain acylates the N-terminus.\n- Residues follow in this order: D-Asn, D-Tyr, D-Trp, D-Orn, L-Orn, Gly, D-Orn, L-Trp, L-Thr, L-Ile, Gly, L-Ser.\n- The macrocycle closes through an ester between the Ser carbonyl and the Thr side-chain oxygen. The ring atoms are Thr C\u03b1, Thr C=O, Ile, Gly, Ser, the ester O and Thr C\u03b2.\n\n**Stereochemistry:**\n- Thr has the L-configuration (2S,3R) and Ile has the L-configuration (2S,3S).\n- The ornithine side chains are plain aminopropyl groups, so only the \u03b1-carbons carry stereo.\n\nI checked the SMILES for ring closures (digits 1 and 2 for the indoles and the tyrosine ring, digit 3 for the macrocycle) and for the atom count against the drawing.\n\nSMILES: CCC(C)CCC(=O)N[C@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@H](Cc1ccc(O)cc1)C(=O)N[C@H](Cc1c[nH]c2ccccc12)C(=O)N[C@H](CCCN)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCN)C(=O)NCC(=O)N[C@H](CCCN)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1c[nH]c2ccccc12)C(=O)N[C@@H]3C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)C(=O)NCC(=O)N[C@@H](CO)C(=O)O[C@@H]3C"
